    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Question\n\nHi, I am trying to recreate the same behavior I got with folke/which-key of mapping Ctrl-r + Ctrl-w when I open a picker (Snacks.picker or Telescope). I want to be able to paste into the buffer whatever is under the cursor (which is the default behavior of n/vim in command mode). Which-key somehow configured this by default also in the picker input, but I can’t find any example configuration for clue.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.clue</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hi, I am trying to recreate the same behavior I got with folke/which-key of mapping Ctrl-r + Ctrl-w when I open a picker (Snacks.picker or Telescope). I want to be able to paste into the buffer whatever is under the cursor (which is the default behavior of n/vim in command mode). Which-key somehow configured this by default also in the picker input, but I can’t find any example configuration for clue.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.clue\nQuestion\nHi, I am trying to recreate the same behavior I got with folke/which-key of mapping Ctrl-r + Ctrl-w when I open a picker (Snacks.picker or Telescope). I want to be able to paste into the buffer whatever is under the cursor (which is the default behavior of n/vim in command mode). Which-key somehow configured this by default also in the picker input, but I can’t find any example configuration for clue.",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-05-22T11:09:11Z",
    "comment_count": 3,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Unfortunately, currently in 'mini.pick' there is no way to use `<C-w>` as the register after `<C-r>`. The best approximation is to manually populate `w` register after every picker start. Something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal populate_registers = function()\r\n  local win_id = MiniPick.get_picker_state().windows.target\r\n  vim.api.nvim_win_call(win_id, function() vim.fn.setreg('w', vim.fn.expand('<cword>')) end)\r\nend\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'MiniPickStart', callback = populate_registers })\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen typing `<C-r>w` will insert \"word under cursor\" from the target window.\r\n\r\nI think support of various `<C-r><C-xxx>` is an interesting idea to add to 'mini.pick'. I'll take a look.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Unfortunately, currently in 'mini.pick' there is no way to use <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-w&gt;</code> as the register after <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-r&gt;</code>. The best approximation is to manually populate <code class=\"notranslate\">w</code> register after every picker start. Something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local populate_registers = function()\n  local win_id = MiniPick.get_picker_state().windows.target\n  vim.api.nvim_win_call(win_id, function() vim.fn.setreg('w', vim.fn.expand('&lt;cword&gt;')) end)\nend\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'MiniPickStart', callback = populate_registers })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">populate_registers</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">win_id</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniPick</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">get_picker_state</span>().<span class=\"pl-e\">windows</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">target</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_win_call</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">win_id</span>, <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fn</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">setreg</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>w<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">fn</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">expand</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;cword&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>)) <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>)\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>User<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>MiniPickStart<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">populate_registers</span> })</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Then typing <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-r&gt;w</code> will insert \"word under cursor\" from the target window.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I think support of various <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-r&gt;&lt;C-xxx&gt;</code> is an interesting idea to add to 'mini.pick'. I'll take a look.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Unfortunately, currently in 'mini.pick' there is no way to use <C-w> as the register after <C-r>. The best approximation is to manually populate w register after every picker start. Something like this:\nlocal populate_registers = function()\n  local win_id = MiniPick.get_picker_state().windows.target\n  vim.api.nvim_win_call(win_id, function() vim.fn.setreg('w', vim.fn.expand('<cword>')) end)\nend\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'MiniPickStart', callback = populate_registers })\nThen typing <C-r>w will insert \"word under cursor\" from the target window.\nI think support of various <C-r><C-xxx> is an interesting idea to add to 'mini.pick'. I'll take a look.",
